  "about": [
    "Which host answers what (deploy/DOMAINS.md). One row per request; each host key is what that host must answer.",
    "Run by: server/test/hostroutes_test.go (the Go handler, part of the Go suite) and deploy/check-domains.py (a real",
    "server: a local binary with Host headers, or the public hosts after a deploy). Written by hand, not derived from the",
    "host table, so the two can disagree and a test says so.",
    "Expectations: \"200\", \"401\", \"404\", or \"301 <Location>\" with {site} and {app} for the configured origins.",
    "Host keys: site, app, api = the configured hosts; site_upper, app_upper = upper-case; app_port = with :443;",
    "unknown = Host: evil.example; fwd_app = Host: evil.example plus X-Forwarded-Host: <app host> (never trusted);",
    "abs_evil = absolute-form request line http://evil.example<path> sent to the server with Host: <app host>.",
    "body_<key>: a substring the body must hold. signed_in: send the app host's session cookie (site and api too).",
    "local_only: needs the test server's own setup (a client tarball, the dev sign-in); skipped against the public hosts."
  ],
